cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EndSurvGAN in your research, please cite this work."
title: "EndSurvGAN: End-to-End Survival-Aware Generative Modeling of Censored Time-to-Event Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Esfandiar
    given-names: Zahra
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zahra-Esfandiar/EndSurvGAN"
url: "https://github.com/Zahra-Esfandiar/EndSurvGAN"
abstract: >-
  EndSurvGAN is a survival-aware generative modeling framework for synthetic
  censored time-to-event data. The work combines adversarial learning with
  survival- and censoring-aware objectives and was accepted as an oral
  presentation at the 18th Iranian Statistics Conference (2026).
keywords:
  - survival analysis
  - censored data
  - generative modeling
  - statistical machine learning
  - synthetic data
  - healthcare data
